From: Pedro Baltazar <pedrobtz@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Initialize the document's quirks mode

new_document_node() initializes every field of GumboDocument except
doc_type_quirks_mode. A document parse sets it when it sees (or misses)
the doctype, but a fragment parse never does, and the "in body" handler
for a <table> start tag reads it to decide whether to close an open <p>.
Fragment parses therefore depend on uninitialized memory, and so does
any caller reading the mode afterwards. Valgrind reports it.

Initialize it to no-quirks, the mode of the document a fragment's context
element is assumed to be in.

Found by running zuhtml's test suite under valgrind. To be offered
upstream at https://codeberg.org/gumbo-parser/gumbo-parser.
---
--- a/parser.c
+++ b/parser.c
@@ -505,6 +505,9 @@
   document->name = NULL;
   document->public_identifier = NULL;
   document->system_identifier = NULL;
+  // A fragment parse never sees a doctype token, but the table start-tag
+  // handler still reads the quirks mode.
+  document->doc_type_quirks_mode = GUMBO_DOCTYPE_NO_QUIRKS;
   return document_node;
 }
 
